'''Module:TimelineRail''' draws a vertical, collapsible timeline. It generates the same markup as the template family {{tl|TimelineRail}} and uses the same stylesheet, <code>Template:TimelineRail/styles.css</code> (loaded with [[mw:Extension:TemplateStyles|TemplateStyles]]), so the look is the same; only the way the HTML is produced changes. It needs no ParserFunctions.

== Entry points ==
Normally the module is used through the templates that call it:
{| class="wikitable"
! Template !! Function !! What it makes
|-
| {{tl|TimelineRail}} || <code>rail</code> || a timeline; <code>|1=</code> holds items and sections; <code>|title=</code> makes it a column
|-
| {{tl|TimelineRail/item}} || <code>item</code> || one dot: <code>date</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>caption</code>, <code>collapsed</code>, <code>collapsible=no</code>, <code>events</code>, <code>sub</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>last</code>
|-
| {{tl|TimelineRail/section}} || <code>section</code> || a titled, collapsible group, nestable; <code>title</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>collapsed</code>, <code>id</code>, and the content in <code>|1=</code>
|-
| {{tl|TimelineRail/event}} || <code>event</code> || one event, for an item with <code>events=</code>
|-
| {{tl|TimelineRail/parallel}} || <code>parallel</code> || timelines side by side; <code>grouped=yes</code> aligns their dots
|-
| {{tl|TimelineRail/gap}} || <code>gap</code> || an empty slot in a grouped column
|-
| {{tl|TimelineRail/outline}} || <code>outline</code> || a whole timeline from one text (below)
|}
The first six take the same parameters as the original templates, so the two families can be swapped.

== Outline: one text, one timeline ==
Item-by-item templates repeat each item's text in every template that wraps it, and a long timeline then exceeds the [[Wikipedia:Template limits|post-expand include size limit]]. <code>outline</code> receives the whole timeline once and builds it once.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
{{TimelineRail/outline
|text=
== Lower Paleolithic ==
The first tools. This line is the section's introduction.
* '''3.3 mya''' Oldest known stone tools.
* '''1.8 mya''' Acheulean hand axes. <ref>...</ref>
** a sub-point, shown as a list
*** a point inside it (<code>***</code>, <code>****</code>, and so on nest further)
[[File:Hand axe.jpg|thumb|A hand axe]]
* 400 kya ;; Fire ;; Controlled use of fire.
=== A section inside it ===
* '''300 kya''' Wooden spears.
== Middle Paleolithic ==
* '''160 kya''' Homo sapiens.
}}
</syntaxhighlight>
{| class="wikitable"
! Line !! Meaning
|-
| <code>== Title ==</code> || a section; <code>===</code> inside it makes a section inside the section, and so on
|-
| plain lines after a heading || the section's introduction, beside its dot
|-
| <code>* '''date''' text</code> || an item: bold date (the usual bullet-list style of articles), then the text
|-
| <code>* date ;; title ;; text</code> || an item with a title; the text may be left out
|-
| <code>**</code> lines || a list inside the item's text
|-
| a line with no marker || continues the line above
|-
| <code>[[File:…]]</code> alone on a line || the picture of the next item
|}
Several <code>[[File:...|caption]]</code> lines before an item put all the pictures on that item, in one row that wraps.

Parameters: <code>open=yes</code>: the rail fades out below the last dot instead of ending there, for a list that is not finished; <code>toc</code>, <code>toclevel</code>: the titles of the sections are real headings of the page, so the table of contents lists them (nested sections one level deeper); <code>toclevel</code> is the level of the top ones (default <code>3</code>, for a timeline under a <code>== Timeline ==</code> heading; 2 to 6) and <code>toc=no</code> makes the titles plain text again; <code>text</code> (or <code>|1=</code>); <code>id</code>, a short prefix for the ids of the items and sections (<code>id=inv2</code> gives <code>inv2_i1</code>, <code>inv2_s1</code>, ...); '''give each outline on a page a different <code>id</code>''' when there is more than one, or their toggles will clash; <code>collapsed=sections</code>, <code>items</code> or <code>all</code> to start closed; <code>title</code> to make it a column of a parallel group. Use <code>|text=</code> when the text contains <code>=</code>; wrap a literal pipe in <code>{{tl|!}}</code>.

